mach-arm-vm_param.patch
Licence: this patch changes a file of Apple's xnu-4570.1.46 (osfmk/mach/arm/vm_param.h) and is under
that release's licence (Apple Public Source License 2.0, APPLE_LICENSE in the release).

What: PAGE_SHIFT, PAGE_SIZE, PAGE_MASK and VM_PAGE_SIZE are the constants of a 4096-byte page
(the file's own PAGE_MIN_SHIFT/PAGE_MIN_SIZE/PAGE_MIN_MASK) instead of the variables vm_page_shift,
vm_page_size and vm_page_mask, and <mach/vm_page_size.h> is no longer included.
Why: xnu-4570.1.46 is the only published release with osfmk/mach/arm, and it is from 2017, when
64-bit ARM devices had 16 KB pages and user code had to read the page size at run time. On the
32-bit ARMv6 devices of iPhone OS 3 the page size was the fixed constant 4096, and code compiled for
them uses it as a constant. With the variables, every use of PAGE_SIZE would load a libSystem
variable that the binaries of this project never imported. <mach/vm_page_size.h> is not installed
in this sysroot (it is a later header, and it declares symbols for iPhone OS 7).
Affects: the units that include <mach/vm_param.h> or <mach/mach.h> through other headers (37 units
of the build); without the change they do not compile.

--- a/usr/include/mach/arm/vm_param.h
+++ b/usr/include/mach/arm/vm_param.h
@@ -37,18 +37,16 @@
 #define _MACH_ARM_VM_PARAM_H_
 
 
-#if !defined (KERNEL) && !defined (__ASSEMBLER__)
-#include <mach/vm_page_size.h>
-#endif
 
 #define BYTE_SIZE	8	/* byte size in bits */
 
 
-#define PAGE_SHIFT			vm_page_shift
-#define PAGE_SIZE			vm_page_size
-#define PAGE_MASK			vm_page_mask
+/* 32-bit ARM, iPhone OS 3: the page size is a constant 4096 bytes */
+#define PAGE_SHIFT			PAGE_MIN_SHIFT
+#define PAGE_SIZE			PAGE_MIN_SIZE
+#define PAGE_MASK			PAGE_MIN_MASK
 
-#define VM_PAGE_SIZE		vm_page_size
+#define VM_PAGE_SIZE		PAGE_MIN_SIZE
 
 #define	machine_ptob(x)		((x) << PAGE_SHIFT)
 
